#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Deterministic run setup: the feature branch, run worktrees, setup commands.

usage:
  python3 setup MANIFEST [--owner TOKEN]

MANIFEST is the run manifest (JSON). setup does what the Setup agent of
run.workflow.js does, without an agent:

A SHA-256 repository (git rev-parse --show-object-format) is refused: exit 3,
nothing changed; the run names commits by 40-hex SHA-1 ids.

git mode (the main checkout repo.root is the feature checkout):
  refuses a main checkout with uncommitted changes (exit 3, nothing created;
  its changes are never discarded), creates repo.branch from repo.base_ref
  unless it exists, and switches the main checkout to repo.branch.
shadow mode (repo.root is not a git repo; repo.git_dir is its shadow):
  creates repo.branch through --git-dir unless it exists and creates or
  reuses the feature worktree <worktree_root>/feature on it. The project
  folder is never modified.

profile full (the default): creates or reuses the lane worktree
<worktree_root>/lane-<id> on branch pl-<run_id>-<id> (new lane branches
start at repo.branch) for every lane. profile lite: no lane worktree or lane
branch; the single lane works in the feature checkout.

Launch lock: setup runs only for the holder of the run's launch lock
(active-run acquire wrote <active dir>/<run_id>.lock; the active dir is
$PL_ACTIVE_DIR, default ${CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR:-~/.claude}/parallel-lanes/active).
It refuses (exit 3, nothing changed) when the lock does not exist or --owner
TOKEN does not match it: without the lock another session may be running
this run, and setup would discard its work.

Checkout lock (git mode only; shadow mode gives each run its own feature
worktree): right after the launch lock check, before any change, setup takes
<active dir>/checkout-<st_dev>-<st_ino>.lock for repo.root, keyed by the
directory's file identity (so a symlink or another spelling of the same
checkout is the same lock, and separate worktrees of one repo are not),
created atomically and holding {"run_id", "checkout"}. A lock of this run
is kept (a relaunch or resume). A lock of another run whose launch lock
still exists is refused (exit 4, naming that run). A lock of another run
without a launch lock is stale: it is renamed aside (one taker wins) and
taken over. An unreadable or malformed checkout lock is refused (exit 4,
naming the file). active-run release and remove delete a run's checkout
locks.

A reused worktree (the run's own: the shadow feature worktree or a lane
worktree) must be a worktree of this repo on its branch. Before its
uncommitted changes are discarded (reset --hard HEAD and clean -fd; ignored
files stay), they are saved. First the staged version: git write-tree on the
worktree's index; when that tree differs from HEAD's it is committed on HEAD
(index_commit). Then every tracked change and untracked, non-ignored file
goes into a commit on top of index_commit (or of HEAD when nothing was
staged), referenced by
refs/parallel-lanes/<run_id>/abandoned/<worktree name>-<UTC time> and listed in
preserved as {"worktree", "ref", "commit", "index_commit": <sha or null>,
"index_saved": <bool>} plus "index_error" (git's message) when index_saved is
false; each discarded change is also listed in discarded as "<worktree>: <git
status --porcelain line>". write-tree on the index can fail (an unmerged
index, a held index.lock): index_saved is then false, the staged version is
not saved, and setup goes on with the working-copy snapshot. A held
index.lock then also fails the reset --hard that follows, so setup exits 1
and the changes stay both in the worktree and in the saved ref. Restore one
in that worktree with git checkout <commit> -- . (the files), then git
read-tree <index_commit> (what was staged; git read-tree HEAD when
index_commit is null: nothing was staged, or, with index_saved false, the
staged version could not be saved). Intent-to-add entries are not
in the index tree and come back untracked. An existing non-empty
directory that is not such a worktree is refused (exit 3) and left alone. No
worktree is removed and no branch is deleted.

Then commands.setup (or the lane's lane_commands override) runs with bash
(the one _shell.find_bash resolves: Git Bash on Windows, never the WSL
launcher; found before any change) in the feature checkout and in each lane
checkout; under lite the lane's own list also runs in the feature checkout
unless it is the same list. Command output goes to stderr.

Under profile full a lane with no pending work keeps its worktree (created
or reused and validated as above) but its setup commands are skipped. A
lane has pending work when some task id in its tasks is not in both the
manifest's done and reviewed lists (absent lists count as empty), as
hasWork/taskState in src/plan.js decide; a lane without tasks has none.
The skipped lanes are listed in setup_skipped in manifest order; a lane
with no setup commands is never listed. The feature checkout's setup always
runs, and profile lite runs every list as before (setup_skipped is []).

Before any change setup removes the records of missing worktrees under
worktree_root (never another worktree's record). repo.base_ref is resolved
to a commit (a leading '-' is refused); the feature branch starts there.

On success setup appends {"task":"_run","event":"run_started","phase":
"setup","head":<feature_head>,"plan_sha256":<sha256 of the plan file>,
"spec_sha256":<sha256 of the spec file, or null>,"setup_skipped":[<lane id>]}
to the ledger lane _run in repo.ledger_dir (ledger status --plan/--spec
compares the hashes on a resume) and prints the manifest's setup_result:
  {"feature_head": <sha of repo.branch>, "worktrees": {<lane id>: <path>},
   "discarded": [...], "preserved": [...], "setup_skipped": [<lane id>]}
The worktree paths are exactly the paths the run uses for the lanes.

On Windows MANIFEST and repo.root, repo.git_dir, repo.worktree_root and
repo.ledger_dir may be in any form (C:\\x, /c/x, /tmp/x); they are used, and
printed, in the C:/... form.

Exit 0 on success; 1 when a git or setup command fails; 2 on a usage error
or an unreadable or malformed manifest (run_id or a lane id outside its
pattern, a relative repo path, a base_ref starting with '-'); 3 on a refused
condition (dirty main checkout, foreign directory or symlink at a run
worktree path, missing shadow, a run locked by another owner, or no bash to
run the setup commands with: the message names CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH);
4 when the checkout is locked by another run, or its checkout lock is
unreadable (nothing changed).
"""

import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import _locks  # noqa: E402
import _owners  # noqa: E402
import _shell  # noqa: E402
import _snapshot  # noqa: E402
from _snapshot import discard_changes, snapshot  # noqa: E402,F401 (snapshot: tests load it from setup)

SCRIPTS = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
# Variables that would point git at another repo than the one named.
GIT_REDIRECTS = ("GIT_DIR", "GIT_WORK_TREE", "GIT_INDEX_FILE",
                 "GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY", "GIT_COMMON_DIR")
ENV = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in GIT_REDIRECTS}
# The same patterns as runIdPattern and laneIdPattern in src/validate.js.
RUN_ID = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9-]+$")
LANE_ID = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$")


# One exception class with _snapshot, whose git steps raise it too.
Failure = _snapshot.Failure


def run_git(args, check=True):
    res = subprocess.run(["git", *args], capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8",
                         errors="surrogateescape", env=ENV)
    if check and res.returncode != 0:
        raise Failure(1, f"git {' '.join(args)} failed: {res.stderr.strip()}")
    return res


def is_text(value):
    return isinstance(value, str) and value != ""


def load_manifest(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            m = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:
        raise Failure(2, f"cannot read manifest {path}: {e}")
    if not isinstance(m, dict):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest must be a JSON object")
    repo = m.get("repo")
    if not isinstance(repo, dict) or repo.get("mode") not in ("git", "shadow"):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest repo.mode must be git or shadow")
    for key in ("root", "base_ref", "branch", "worktree_root", "ledger_dir"):
        if not is_text(repo.get(key)):
            raise Failure(2, f"manifest repo.{key} must be a non-empty string")
    if repo["mode"] == "shadow" and not is_text(repo.get("git_dir")):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest repo.git_dir is required in shadow mode")
    paths = ("root", "worktree_root", "ledger_dir") + (("git_dir",) if repo["mode"] == "shadow" else ())
    for key in paths:
        repo[key] = _shell.native_path(repo[key])
        if not os.path.isabs(repo[key]):
            raise Failure(2, f"manifest repo.{key} must be an absolute path")
    if repo["base_ref"].startswith("-"):
        raise Failure(2, f"manifest repo.base_ref must not start with '-': {repo['base_ref']!r}")
    if not is_text(m.get("run_id")) or not RUN_ID.fullmatch(m["run_id"]):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest run_id must use only a-z, 0-9 and -")
    lanes = m.get("lanes")
    if not isinstance(lanes, list) or not all(
            isinstance(lane, dict) and is_text(lane.get("id")) for lane in lanes):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest lanes must be a list of objects with an id")
    for lane in lanes:
        if not LANE_ID.fullmatch(lane["id"]) or lane["id"] in ("prelude", "join"):
            raise Failure(2, f"manifest lane id {lane['id']!r} is not a safe lane id")
    if m.get("profile", "full") not in ("full", "lite"):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest profile must be lite or full")
    if not isinstance(m.get("commands"), dict):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest commands must be an object")
    for branch in [repo["branch"]] + [lane_branch(m, lane) for lane in lanes]:
        ok = run_git(["check-ref-format", "--branch", branch], check=False)
        if ok.returncode != 0 or branch.startswith("-"):
            raise Failure(2, f"invalid branch name {branch!r}")
    return m


def setup_commands(m, lane_id):
    """The setup list for a lane (None: the feature checkout), as commandList."""
    own = (m.get("lane_commands") or {}).get(lane_id) if lane_id is not None else None
    if isinstance(own, dict) and "setup" in own:
        cmds = own["setup"]
    else:
        cmds = m["commands"].get("setup") or []
    if not isinstance(cmds, list) or not all(is_text(c) for c in cmds):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest setup commands must be lists of non-empty strings")
    return cmds


def lane_pending(m, lane):
    """True when some task of the lane is not in both done and reviewed.

    Mirrors hasWork/taskState in src/plan.js: a task not done runs, a done
    but unreviewed task is reviewed, only a done and reviewed task is
    skipped. A lane without tasks has no pending work.
    """
    done = m.get("done") if isinstance(m.get("done"), list) else []
    reviewed = m.get("reviewed") if isinstance(m.get("reviewed"), list) else []
    tasks = lane.get("tasks") if isinstance(lane.get("tasks"), list) else []
    return any(not (isinstance(t, dict) and t.get("id") in done and t.get("id") in reviewed)
               for t in tasks)


def feature_dir(m):
    repo = m["repo"]
    return f"{repo['worktree_root']}/feature" if repo["mode"] == "shadow" else repo["root"]


def lane_dir(m, lane):
    return f"{m['repo']['worktree_root']}/lane-{lane['id']}"


def lane_branch(m, lane):
    return f"pl-{m['run_id']}-{lane['id']}"


class Repo:
    """git commands against the run's repo (main checkout or shadow git dir)."""

    def __init__(self, m):
        repo = m["repo"]
        if repo["mode"] == "shadow":
            git_dir = repo["git_dir"]
            if not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(git_dir, "pl-baseline")):
                raise Failure(3, f"not a shadow git dir: {git_dir}")
            self.prefix = [f"--git-dir={git_dir}"]
        else:
            if not os.path.isdir(repo["root"]):
                raise Failure(2, f"repo.root is not a directory: {repo['root']}")
            self.prefix = ["-C", repo["root"]]
        top = self.git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir", check=False)
        if top.returncode != 0:
            raise Failure(2, f"not a git repo: {' '.join(self.prefix)}: {top.stderr.strip()}")
        self.common_dir = os.path.realpath(top.stdout.strip())

    def git(self, *args, check=True):
        return run_git([*self.prefix, *args], check=check)

    def has_branch(self, branch):
        res = self.git("show-ref", "--verify", "--quiet", f"refs/heads/{branch}", check=False)
        return res.returncode == 0

    def head_of(self, branch):
        return self.git("rev-parse", "--verify", f"refs/heads/{branch}^{{commit}}").stdout.strip()

    def resolve(self, ref):
        """The commit sha ref names; git never reads ref as an option."""
        res = self.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--end-of-options", f"{ref}^{{commit}}", check=False)
        if res.returncode != 0:
            raise Failure(1, f"repo.base_ref {ref!r} does not name a commit: {res.stderr.strip()}")
        return res.stdout.strip()

    def prune_run_worktrees(self, root):
        """Remove the records of missing worktrees under root (the run's own).

        Records of the user's other worktrees, missing or not, are left alone.
        """
        roots = {os.path.normpath(root), os.path.realpath(root)}
        listing = self.git("worktree", "list", "--porcelain").stdout
        for block in listing.split("\n\n"):
            lines = block.splitlines()
            if not lines or not lines[0].startswith("worktree "):
                continue
            path = lines[0][len("worktree "):]
            if not any(line == "prunable" or line.startswith("prunable ") for line in lines[1:]):
                continue
            norm = os.path.normpath(path)
            if os.path.isabs(norm) and any(norm.startswith(r + os.sep) for r in roots):
                self.git("worktree", "remove", norm)


def worktree_state(repo, path, branch):
    """'missing' (absent or empty dir) or 'reuse'; raises on anything else.

    A symlink is always refused, even one to an empty directory: git would
    create the worktree at the link's target, outside worktree_root.
    """
    refuse = Failure(3, f"{path} exists and is not a worktree of this repo on {branch}; "
                        "move it away or fix it by hand")
    if os.path.islink(path):
        raise refuse
    if not os.path.lexists(path) or (os.path.isdir(path) and not os.listdir(path)):
        return "missing"
    if not os.path.isdir(path):
        raise refuse
    top = run_git(["-C", path, "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute",
                   "--show-toplevel", "--git-common-dir"], check=False)
    if top.returncode != 0:
        raise refuse
    toplevel, common = top.stdout.splitlines()[:2]
    if (os.path.realpath(toplevel) != os.path.realpath(path)
            or os.path.realpath(common) != repo.common_dir):
        raise refuse
    head = run_git(["-C", path, "symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD"], check=False)
    if head.returncode != 0 or head.stdout.strip() != branch:
        raise refuse
    return "reuse"


def check_lock(run_id, owner):
    """Refuse unless the run's launch lock exists and owner matches it."""
    lock = os.path.join(_locks.active_dir(), f"{run_id}.lock")
    try:
        with open(lock, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            token = f.read().strip()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise Failure(3, f"run {run_id} has no launch lock ({lock}); run active-run acquire first and pass its "
                         "token as --owner (nothing was changed)")
    except OSError as e:
        raise Failure(3, f"cannot read the launch lock {lock}: {e}")
    if owner is None or owner != token:
        raise Failure(3, f"run {run_id} is locked by another launch ({lock}); another session may still be "
                         "running it, so nothing was changed. If it has ended, run active-run acquire with "
                         "--takeover and pass the new token as --owner")


def checkout_lock(m):
    """Take the checkout lock of repo.root for this run (git mode), as
    _locks.checkout_lock does; its LockError becomes a Failure with the
    same code and message."""
    try:
        _locks.checkout_lock(m["repo"]["root"], m["run_id"])
    except _locks.LockError as e:
        raise Failure(e.code, str(e))


def file_sha256(path):
    if not is_text(path):
        return None
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            return hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        # Recorded as null: a resume cannot then tell whether it changed.
        return None
    except OSError as e:
        raise Failure(2, f"cannot read {path}: {e}")


def ensure_worktree(repo, path, branch, start, state, run_id, discarded, preserved):
    if state == "reuse":
        discard_changes(path, run_id, discarded, preserved)
        return
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    if repo.has_branch(branch):
        repo.git("worktree", "add", "-q", path, branch)
    else:
        repo.git("worktree", "add", "-q", "-b", branch, path, start)


def check_branch(path, branch):
    head = run_git(["-C", path, "rev-parse", "--abbrev-ref", "HEAD"]).stdout.strip()
    if head != branch:
        raise Failure(1, f"{path} is on {head}, expected {branch}")


def run_commands(path, cmds):
    for cmd in cmds:
        res = subprocess.run(_shell.bash_argv("-c", cmd), cwd=path, env=ENV,
                             stdout=sys.stderr, stderr=sys.stderr)
        if res.returncode != 0:
            raise Failure(1, f"setup command failed in {path} (exit {res.returncode}): {cmd}")


def setup(m, owner=None):
    check_lock(m["run_id"], owner)
    repo_cfg = m["repo"]
    if repo_cfg["mode"] == "git":
        checkout_lock(m)
    lite = m.get("profile", "full") == "lite"
    branch = repo_cfg["branch"]
    repo = Repo(m)
    feature = feature_dir(m)

    # Every refusal comes before the first change.
    # The run names commits by 40-hex SHA-1 ids (isSha): a SHA-256 repository
    # would fail partway through. Only an explicit sha256 answer refuses, so
    # an old git that does not know the option is not refused by mistake.
    object_format = repo.git("rev-parse", "--show-object-format", check=False).stdout.strip()
    if object_format == "sha256":
        raise Failure(3, "the repository uses SHA-256 object names; parallel-lanes supports only SHA-1 "
                         "repositories (nothing was changed)")
    if repo_cfg["mode"] == "git":
        dirty = run_git(["-C", feature, "status", "--porcelain"]).stdout
        if dirty:
            raise Failure(3, f"the main checkout {feature} has uncommitted changes; commit or "
                             f"stash them first (nothing was changed):\n{dirty.rstrip()}")
    feature_state = (worktree_state(repo, feature, branch)
                     if repo_cfg["mode"] == "shadow" else None)
    lanes = [] if lite else [(lane, lane_dir(m, lane), lane_branch(m, lane)) for lane in m["lanes"]]
    lane_states = [worktree_state(repo, path, lb) for _, path, lb in lanes]
    if any(setup_commands(m, lane_id) for lane_id in [None] + [lane["id"] for lane in m["lanes"]]):
        _shell.find_bash()

    base = repo.resolve(repo_cfg["base_ref"])

    discarded = []
    preserved = []
    # Drops only the records of the run's own worktrees whose directory is gone.
    repo.prune_run_worktrees(repo_cfg["worktree_root"])
    if not repo.has_branch(branch):
        repo.git("branch", branch, base)
    if repo_cfg["mode"] == "git":
        repo.git("switch", "-q", branch)
    else:
        ensure_worktree(repo, feature, branch, base, feature_state, m["run_id"], discarded, preserved)
    check_branch(feature, branch)
    for (_, path, lb), state in zip(lanes, lane_states):
        ensure_worktree(repo, path, lb, branch, state, m["run_id"], discarded, preserved)
        check_branch(path, lb)

    feature_cmds = setup_commands(m, None)
    run_commands(feature, feature_cmds)
    if lite:
        for lane in m["lanes"]:
            cmds = setup_commands(m, lane["id"])
            if cmds != feature_cmds:
                run_commands(feature, cmds)
    # A lane with no pending work keeps its worktree but not its setup run;
    # a lane without setup commands had nothing to skip and is not listed.
    skipped = []
    for lane, path, _ in lanes:
        cmds = setup_commands(m, lane["id"])
        if cmds and not lane_pending(m, lane):
            skipped.append(lane["id"])
            continue
        run_commands(path, cmds)

    head = repo.head_of(branch)
    entry = {"task": "_run", "event": "run_started", "phase": "setup", "head": head,
             "plan_sha256": file_sha256(m.get("plan")), "spec_sha256": file_sha256(m.get("spec")),
             "setup_skipped": skipped}
    res = subprocess.run([sys.executable, os.path.join(SCRIPTS, "ledger"), "append",
                          repo_cfg["ledger_dir"], "_run", json.dumps(entry)],
                         capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace", env=ENV)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise Failure(1, f"ledger append failed: {res.stderr.strip()}")
    # The owner map start-task --owners and ledger owners read (1.6.3): which
    # tasks list each path, and where each task runs.
    owners_file = os.path.join(repo_cfg["ledger_dir"], "owners.json")
    try:
        _shell.write_text(owners_file + ".tmp", json.dumps(_owners.build(m), indent=2) + "\n")
        os.replace(owners_file + ".tmp", owners_file)
    except OSError as e:
        raise Failure(1, f"cannot write the owner map {owners_file!r}: {e}")
    worktrees = {lane["id"]: feature if lite else lane_dir(m, lane) for lane in m["lanes"]}
    return {"feature_head": head, "worktrees": worktrees, "discarded": discarded, "preserved": preserved,
            "setup_skipped": skipped}


def main(argv):
    _shell.setup_io()
    try:
        owner = None
        if len(argv) == 3 and argv[1] == "--owner" and argv[2]:
            owner = argv[2]
        elif len(argv) != 1:
            raise Failure(2, "usage: setup MANIFEST [--owner TOKEN]")
        if not argv[0]:
            raise Failure(2, "usage: setup MANIFEST [--owner TOKEN]")
        result = setup(load_manifest(_shell.native_path(argv[0])), owner)
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        print(f"setup: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(3)
    except Failure as e:
        print(f"setup: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(e.code)
    print(json.dumps(result))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
